  "_about": "Seed for scripts/gen-identities.py: what varies between real users of one browser version besides the phone model. Every list names its source; nothing here is a guess. Chrome builds: chromiumdash.appspot.com/fetch_releases (Stable, Windows), read 2026-09-22. Windows platform versions: Sec-CH-UA-Platform-Version is the Windows.Foundation.UniversalApiContract version (learn.microsoft.com/microsoft-edge/web-platform/how-to-detect-win11; Chromium components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc, highest known contract 19) — 10.0.0 for Windows 10 22H2 measured on the capture machine (STAGE19), 13/14/15 for Windows 11 21H2/22H2/23H2, 19.0.0 for 24H2. macOS versions: Wikipedia release tables of macOS Sequoia (15) and Tahoe (26), read 2026-09-22; Chromium reports the version with dots. iOS versions: Wikipedia release tables of iOS 18 and iOS 26, read 2026-09-22; Safari 18 on iOS writes the OS version into the User-Agent twice, iPhone OS 18_1_1 and Version/18.1.1 (real strings on useragents.io and user-agents.net). Safari 26 froze the OS token at 18_7 and writes the real version only in Version/: every 26.0, 26.0.1, 26.1, 26.2, 26.3 and 26.5 observed in real traffic (user-agents.net, useragents.io, deviceandbrowserinfo.com, read 2026-09-22) says iPhone OS 18_7; frozen_os carries that. Updated 2026-09-26: Chrome 153 builds .37 .48 .54 .55 and the 154 builds (chromiumdash, Stable); macOS platform versions with three parts, as Chromium formats them (%d.%d.%d in user_agent_utils.cc GetPlatformVersion), and macOS 27.0 (Apple silicon only); Safari 26.0 on iOS pins the OS token at 18_6 (Leenheer, 51Degrees), 26.0.1 and later at 18_7.",
